    "body": "The single frozen comparison completed `CLAUSE_ADAPTER_PRESERVED`: raw text now has empirical qualification at the accepted reader/core boundary for the fixed known-vocabulary, fixed-query, four-fact grammar. All 1,600 valid rows matched the independent segmented reference across inputs and complete compared tensors. All 96 refusal/boundary cases matched with zero model forwards. Full deterministic and oracle identities replayed exactly in fresh processes.\n\nThe result covers twenty already-observed base semantic groups and their related renderings. Each arm/phase returned 1,600 correct answers and 22,400 correct consumed roles. Total work was 6,400 logical forwards and zero optimizer updates, with 15.821630625 seconds operator wall time. The final cumulative snapshot includes the historical 120-second policy debit. Source, model, population, runtime and frozen criteria were unchanged; the one-shot envelope is consumed.\n\nThis delivers the activation/operator receipts, original result/replay/progress/resource copies, source and independent result reviews, claim ledger, current roadmap and #1086 contract-only handoff. Earlier unavailable, runtime-only, weak-control and descriptive results remain preserved. It adds no mathematical proof, new-world/general-language result, native export or final serving-kernel qualification.\n\nValidation: the one authorized comparison and fresh-process replay; independent original-receipt integrity/DoD review; independent delivery/ledger review; claim-wording and diff-whitespace checks. Broad QA remains dormant under current AGENTS.md. Protected statuses acknowledge transport and do not supply scientific evidence.\n\nStorage: withheld inputs are resealed. Seventeen original receipts remain. The frozen consumer removed its two temporary oracle streams after persisting phase evidence; this raw temporary data is no longer retained, as recorded explicitly. No other cleanup or model run followed.\n\nReferences #1094. Close after verified protected merge and completion comment. #973 remains open and #954 blocked. Next action is the separately activated #1086 export/loader/reference-behavior specification before implementation; no work on that specification is included here.\n",
